    <fr:title text="Using Local Sections to Construct Natural Isomorphisms">Using Local Sections to Construct Natural Isomorphisms</fr:title>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>Given categories <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[C]]></fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[D]]></fr:tex> with functors <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F , G : D \to  C]]></fr:tex>,
the data of a natural isomorphism <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F \cong  G]]></fr:tex> is precisely the same
data of a local section of <fr:link href="/sss-0067/" title="Displayed Category of Isomorphisms" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-0067/" display-uri="sss-0067" type="local">the displayed category of isomorphisms</fr:link>.</html:p>
    <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[s : D \times  D \to _{{\mathopen {}\left (F , G\right )\mathclose {}}} \mathsf {Iso_{C}}]]></fr:tex>
  </fr:mainmatter>
